## The Natural 1ct Threshold

This is the first hidden spec at the $5K level. It's the answer to "why does $5K feel different from $4K?"

At $4,000, the cheapest GIA natural 1ct marquise in certified inventory is $4,049. No setting budget left. At $5,000, you have $951 for a setting. That's enough for a real solitaire. Combo 1 proves it.

Here's what the natural 1ct threshold looks like in practice:

| Stone grade | GIA natural 1ct price | Setting budget left at $5K | Can you build a ring? |
|---|---|---|---|
| I VS2 | $4,049 | $951 | Yes — solitaire $860 → total $4,909 |
| I VS1 | $4,123 | $877 | Yes — solitaire $860 → total $4,983 |
| H VS2 | $4,393 | $607 | Tight — cheapest solitaire available |
| H VS1 | $4,629 | $371 | No room for a real setting |
| **What this means** | I color is the sweet spot | $5K unlocks I VS2 and I VS1 | G or H color requires more budget |

I color isn't a "lesser" grade in white gold. It reads visually identical to G or H in a cool metal setting. The [marquise diamond color guide](/marquise-diamond-color-guide) breaks down the exact visual difference by metal type.

For the full comparison of natural stones at this price range, see our [GIA-certified marquise diamond](/gia-certified-marquise-diamond) guide.

